 Splunk Practical 01: Baseline Data Inventory (B1)

1. Objective & Scope
Objective: Perform baseline data discovery and telemetry classification on ingested index streams using Search Processing Language (SPL).
Environment: Splunk Enterprise (Windows Local Instance)
Target Index: `_internal` (System Diagnostic & Access Telemetry)
 2. Practical Execution: Data Inventory
 SPL Query Executed
index=_internal earliest=-7d
| stats count by sourcetype
| sort - count

SPL Query Explanation
index=_internal : Splunk ke internal diagnostics aur operational log storage ko search target banata hai.

earliest=-7d : Pichle 7 din ka time window filter karta hai taaki purane data ki scanning na ho aur performance fast rahe.

| stats count by sourcetype : Raw log events ko pipe karke har unique log type (sourcetype) ke total events ka count calculate karta hai aur table banata hai.

| sort - count : Minus (-) sign ke sath count ko descending order me sort karta hai taaki sabse zyada logs generate karne wale sources sabse upar dikhein.
